---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="What this publication is, and the rule it holds itself to.">
  <article>
    <header class="article-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Every field has sentences it repeats. <em>Advertising is salesmanship in print.
        Niche down. Add value. Trust the process.</em> They get quoted because they were
        once true enough to survive — and repeated until nobody checks which half still is.
      </p>
      <p>
        This publication tests them. Each piece takes one received sentence, puts it under
        an instrument, and keeps pressing until the missing half falls out. Sometimes the
        sentence holds and the test shows <em>why</em> it holds, which is rarer knowledge
        than it sounds. Sometimes it breaks, and the break is the article.
      </p>
      <p>
        The house rule: <strong>publish the test, not just the flip.</strong> A contrarian
        sentence is the easiest thing in the world to write; the receipts are what make it
        worth your time. If a piece here ever asks you to take its word for something, it
        has failed its own standard — write in and say so.
      </p>
      <p><em>New issues land weekly, sometimes faster. Subscribe by RSS below.</em></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
